{
  "_about": "v1.360.0 lane 10A: ONE notice per run outcome. Each case is a persisted event (the audit's shape: id, type, session_id, ts, payload). `pings` = the dashboard bell raises a desktop ping for it while a window is open (so the daemon keeps 'This PC' quiet: comm/notifier.bell_pings); `attention` = it counts on the bell's badge, and the desktop app says it while it sits in the tray (comm/notifier.bell_attention, desktop/main.js runOutcomeNotice); `title` / `body` / `href` = the bell row's words, which the tray notice repeats. Read by tests/test_one_notice_v13600.py (Python + main.js under node) and dashboard/__tests__/one-notice-v13600.test.tsx (the real bell). v1.374.0 (IJ harness part 2, Phase 3): a Build turn that ran longer than a minute and ended (`build.turn_finished`) is a ringing row too, said from the tray once; `phone` (default true) = the default notifier also sends it to a phone destination; a Build turn's notice is desktop only (not a default alert). v1.392.0 (the long-jobs plan's Phase 3): a Build reply that made no progress for ten minutes (`build.turn_stalled`, once per stall episode) rings the same way and is said from the tray once; desktop only (not a default alert).",
